+# Previous tracks retained in Google Cloud — 2026-10-06
+
+Requirements B01–B07/B19/B20/B23/R01/Q01. The owner confirmed Google sign-in works and requested keeping the previous tracks. **All 27 previous official tracks are now in the cloud catalog**, with their existing “Beat my track” attribution. The original WSL services and data remain intact.
+
+Every logical track UUID, name, authoring ID and current document hash is preserved. All **34 original published version UUIDs/share links** still return their original hash-checked bytes. Twenty-six old heads used physics arcade-planar-0.49 / rules standing-5-road-gates-v14; the current deployed build uses arcade-planar-0.50 / standing-5-road-gates-v18. Those heads received **26 additional immutable revisions**, using the same document bytes and manifests generated by the real deployed native validator. Old manifests/links were not rewritten. Cloud now has 27 logical tracks, 60 published revisions and 34 unique documents.
+
+Restored: Ajorata, Blind spot, Curvy, Dust cloud, Dusty, Easy night, Ellipse, Infinity, Knit, Knot, Lonkero, Looper, My way, Narrow night, Over and under, Ringroad, Saw, Sightseeing, Silmukka, Slippery, Speedy, Spiral, Starter Circuit, Stormy slalom, The Wall, To the trees and Underpass.
+
+## Transfer and account boundaries
+
+The operator importer adds to the existing destination and preserves the Google account/session data. Catalog attribution has no login identities, credentials, races, rivalry membership or rewards. No development identity/session, artificial driver, personal best, rating, ghost, wallet or entitlement was copied. All 27 source tracks were already official; that flag is preserved. No invented creator run or time was created. Player-facing publishing retains its normal verified creator test.
+
+The importer checks the confirmed source, bounded unique IDs/revision numbers, canonical object hashes, official attribution, collisions and every current head. It refuses adoption of an authenticated destination account. Compatible revision UUIDs/keys are deterministic from source version plus manifest, with one fixed migration timestamp. The actual retry inserted **zero tracks and zero versions**. Native validation and immutable object IO hold no DB locks; metadata inserts commit as one transaction.
+
+The read-only local export contains only public catalog data: 27 tracks, 34 versions and 34 documents. The ignored snapshot is .tools/gcp-track-transfer/source-catalog.json, SHA256 f3040a3cc045100b8ecc742836d6a8e978b3613042f63d3bf0e37ba7f03e1e63. It contains no login credentials/subjects; originals were not deleted or rewritten.
+
+An owned one-off job, bmt-stg-e7a444ab-catalog, used the existing pinned image sha256:bec69858e2a6d2494d96a0169076f8e2f497c84f9d36e0ebb5dd02a8c0fdbca0, restricted app DB role and attached diagnostic ADC. The private GCS transfer artifact and operator-authored program are hash-checked before execution; user documents supply JSON data only. API/worker images, schemas, canonical simulation, dependencies and HTTP authentication are unchanged.
+
+## Retention replaces temporary deletion
+
+The owner’s request supersedes the disposable cleanup deadline. Windows task BMT-staging-cleanup-e7a444ab is **disabled**. The first process match missed Windows backslash paths; the final normalized-path check verified and stopped both Python processes for this exact owned watcher. The main/frozen configurations set retain_data=true. Cleanup refuses that local hold before cloud calls and also checks the remote bmt-retain-data=true label during the all-resource preflight, before any deletion. SQL has that label and provider deletion protection.
+
+Daily standard SQL backups run at **02:00 UTC**, retaining seven daily backups. Manual backups immediately **before and after migration both completed SUCCESSFUL**. GCS recovery for accidentally deleted objects is enabled for **seven days**, verified as 604800 seconds. Original WSL data and the immutable export are independent track copies. Full backup-restore/production DR acceptance remains unperformed; point-in-time recovery was not enabled.
+
+This is retained staging, not an approved production rollout. Historical lease labels no longer authorize deletion while the retention hold is active. Future deployment/pricing reviews still need current configuration. Keeping it running uses credits: recorded regional EUR rates imply roughly **€2.4/day baseline before credits/free tier**, plus API use, backups, object/registry storage and network. [Calculation](evidence/gcp-track-retention-2026-10-06/retained-cost-estimate.json), [Cloud Run pricing](https://cloud.google.com/run/pricing). The existing €10 monthly project alert remains an alert rather than a cap. Exact remaining credits/expiry and actual bill were not checked; the owner’s approximate €300/80-day report remains the source. No paid-account upgrade or commitment was made.
+
+## Actual commands and outcomes
+
+Project beat-my-track and region europe-west1 were explicit in all SDK operations. Commands from repository root used .tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe with the ignored helpers:
+
+~~~text
+.tools/gcp-staging/export-local-catalog.py
+.tools/gcp-staging/run-catalog-transfer.py retain
+.tools/gcp-staging/run-catalog-transfer.py prepare
+.tools/gcp-staging/run-catalog-transfer.py validate
+.tools/gcp-staging/run-catalog-transfer.py import
+# Same import repeated to prove zero-insert retry.
+.tools/gcp-staging/verify-retained-catalog.py
+~~~
+
+Additional actual commands:
+
+~~~powershell
+& .tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest backend/tests/test_catalog_transfer.py backend/tests/test_gcp_staging.py -q
+& .tools/backend-venv/Scripts/ruff.exe check backend/deploy/gcp/catalog_transfer.py backend/tests/test_catalog_transfer.py backend/deploy/gcp/staging.py backend/tests/test_gcp_staging.py
+powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_retained_cloud_catalog.gd -Graphical -CommandTimeoutSeconds 300
+~~~
+
+- Final unit regression: **34 passed**. Tests cover dry-run purity, corrupt hashes, authenticated-owner protection, existing-account/session preservation, immutable collisions, historical bytes, deterministic compatible revisions and local/remote retention holds.
+- The first cloud dry run failed before catalog reads/writes: broad placeholder substitution altered the BMT_STAGING_OWNER environment-key name. Explicit delimited placeholders fixed the launcher. Corrected native validation passed: 27 current heads, 34 objects, 60 planned versions and 26 compatible revisions.
+- First live import: **27 tracks/60 versions inserted**. Live retry: **0/0 inserted**, same IDs. Public HTTP verification checked **27 current entries and all 34 original share links** against original SHA256 documents.
+- Initial real Windows graphical app check: 166 checks pass. Final strengthened check: **167 checks, zero failures**, including normal pagination, 27 downloads/compilations, native/server geometry hashes, current physics/rules and selection with Race enabled. Runs overlap. Isolated guest records/cache avoid reading the owner’s saved Google session.
+- [Actual restored Race screenshot with Spiral selected](evidence/gcp-track-retention-2026-10-06/race-catalog.png) saved and inspected.
+- Provider state: SQL RUNNABLE, deletion/retention protection true, daily backups/seven-day object recovery configured, and both manual backups SUCCESSFUL.
+- Ruff initially requested combining a nested conditional. The equivalent combined guard passes lint and the final 34 tests. The exact live executed program is retained in evidence; this final lint-only edit did not change runtime images or imported data.
+- Final task-state/path-normalized process check confirms automatic deletion remains disabled; the original WSL API/worker/database remain running. Affected whitespace and scoped-patch reverse checks exit zero, with existing CRLF normalization warnings only.
+
+## Files and remaining acceptance
+
+Changed source: backend/deploy/gcp/catalog_transfer.py, backend/deploy/gcp/staging.py, backend/tests/test_catalog_transfer.py, backend/tests/test_gcp_staging.py and game/tests/test_retained_cloud_catalog.gd. The game check is opt-in and excluded by the existing tests/* export filter. Documentation: this report, staging runbook/prior connection/deployment notes, development/phase status and [evidence/checkpoint](evidence/gcp-track-retention-2026-10-06/README.md). Ignored .tools helpers/config/artifacts contain applied operator state and the source export; credentials are excluded from Git.
+
+No phone attachment check, Android export/install or physical-device test was performed. No complete race on every circuit, old PB/ratings identity migration, measured capacity, NAS rollout or production acceptance is claimed. Google login success is owner-reported; the operator did not obtain a Google ID token. Local scores remain local. Reopen Race or restart the app to refresh its public catalog; no player file is deleted to force refresh.
